      "evidence": "template/scripts/post_review_finalization.py, `rederive_archived_specs`: `set(workers._git(checkout, \"diff\", \"--name-only\", \"--diff-filter=U\").split()) - spec_paths` and the `both` computation use whitespace splitting. `derived_merge_only` uses `splitlines()` with the same quoting problem. By contrast, `validate_finalization_paths` and `execute_finalize` use `-z`. These checks gate which paths are treated as archive-derived, so they should use NUL-delimited output as the finalization checks do. The `outside` conflict guard fails closed on an odd path because the odd path then cannot be in `spec_paths`. The `both - spec_paths` guard can be defeated only in unusual cases.",
